cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the upstream work it builds on."
title: "smolvla_flow_rl: online reinforcement learning fine tuning for flow matching vision language action policies"
abstract: >-
  An engineering substrate for online reinforcement learning fine tuning of a flow matching vision language
  action policy on a single consumer GPU. Provides a stochastic sampler that yields a tractable action
  likelihood without modifying the pretrained action head, a policy gradient update that grades the executed
  action, a process isolated simulator harness with a sparse terminal reward, a deterministic evaluation entry
  point with a completeness gate, and a written verification protocol.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Yardimci"
    given-names: "Mehmet Turan"
license: Apache-2.0
# The release date rather than a bare year: CFF 1.2.0 has no year key at the root, and a file carrying one is
# rejected by the schema. Renderers take the year from here, so APA and BibTeX both read 2026.
date-released: "2026-07-29"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mturan33/smolvla_flow_rl"
url: "https://github.com/mturan33/smolvla_flow_rl"
keywords:
  - robotics
  - reinforcement learning
  - vision language action
  - flow matching
  - reproducibility

